  "notes": "University Park. 'Engineering elective', 'Professional elective', 'Chemical engineering elective', 'Science elective', 'Science or engineering elective', and 'Lab experience' pools (26 credits total) are modeled generically, same convention as CMPSC's own open pools. Post-prereq-parser-fix repair: CHEM 110's real prereq is MATH 22, which was never in this plan -- and MATH 22 itself real-chains through MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3, none of which were present either, leaving CHEM 110 (and everything after it: CHEM 111/112/113/210/212/213, then CHE 210/220/320/330) permanently unschedulable. Added MATH 3/MATH 4 (Semester 1) and MATH 21/MATH 22 (Semester 2) explicitly to complete the real chain. FLAGGED FOR HUMAN REVIEW: even with this real, catalog-confirmed fix, the plan no longer completes in 4 years (8 terms) -- it needs 10. The MATH 3->4->21->22 chain (4 sequential terms, unavoidable: none of these have concurrent_groups) pushes CHEM 110 to term 5, and CHE's own already-tight critical path needs 5 more sequential terms after that (CHEM 110 -> CHEM 112 -> CHE 210/CHEM 210 -> CHE 220/320/330 -> CHE 410/430 -> CHE 470/480W). This isn't purely a credit-capacity issue (several simulated terms land well under the existing 18cr cap) -- it's the length of the real prereq chain itself. Verified clean (no warnings, goal met) at grad_years=6 (10 simulated terms / 5 years). Not patched further here since doing so would require either dropping a real requirement or inventing a substitute path not supported by the actual catalog data.",
